+## Task ID: 3-a — Agent: letter-a-expansion (orchestrator session)
+
+Added support for every verifiably real file-format extension starting with the letter **a**, as a lazily-loaded registry expansion. Honest scope note: the requested "10,000+ real A-extensions" do not exist in any authoritative database (FileInfo ~420 A-rows, FileExt ~790 A-rows, Wikipedia ~190, registries fewer); the complete cross-source union after dedup against the existing DB is 718 new extensions, bringing A-coverage from 353 → **1,061** (total catalog 5,891 → 6,609 extensions, 4,940 records, 10,727 identities).
+
+- **New file `src/lib/formats/a-expansion.ts`** (718 `RawFormat` records, ~96 KB chunk): generated by `scripts/build_a_expansion.py` from 7 engineering sources — fileinfo.com letter-A index, filext.com letter-A list, Wikipedia filename-extension list, mime-db (IANA), Apache Tika registry, freedesktop shared-mime-info 1.10, dyne/file-extension-list (corroboration) — plus the two real split-volume conventions (ALZip .a00-.a99, split(1) .aa-.az) per the families.ts policy. 204 records verified in ≥2 independent sources ("verified in N sources" in desc). Provenance: descriptions are short factual identifications from the named public databases; no invented entries (spot-checked via web search: a000 Camtasia, a018 Redemption, aamv Alipay Ant Forest, a1 Free Pascal all confirmed).
+- **Classification**: two-stage keyword classifier — primary meaning (name+desc) first; multi-meaning fallback text only if primary yields nothing, with secondary matches routed to the safe `fallback` viewer. Vendor parens stripped before matching ("(Vector)" no longer implies vector graphics); viewer spread: fallback 370, archive 86, image 67, code 55, text 38, video 35, audio 34, eml 16, rest niche.
+- **Lazy loading (`formats/index.ts`)**: registries are now module-level mutable objects; new `registerRawFormats()` merges with first-extension-wins (curated records keep priority), bumps `FORMATS_VERSION`, emits `formats-events`. New `ensureFormatsLoaded()` dynamic-imports the chunk once; `addFiles` awaits it before detection so an instant drop can never miss the expansion. Chunk split verified in `next build` output (not in main bundle).
+- **`formats/stats.ts`**: FORMAT_STATS/EXPLORER_ROWS are mutated in place on registration (Object.assign + splice) — no ESM live-binding reliance; `FORMATS_STATS_VERSION.n` counter drives memo invalidation in format-explorer (rows + category filter) and app-shell's landing count-up badge, which now animates to the bigger number once the chunk lands.
+- **Coherence fix**: addToIndex skips records whose every extension is already mapped — removed 52 previously-unreachable duplicate records from FORMAT_RECORDS (EXT_MAP unchanged; explorer rows deduped).
+- **Verification**: `tsc --noEmit` 0 errors; `next build` clean (static export, 4 pages); runtime merge test: 5,891→6,609 extensions / 0 unresolved expansion exts / 0 dup keys; detection smoke test (song.a2b→Adlib Tracker [audio/midi], backup.ab→Android adb Backup [archive], map.axe→AutoRoute Map [geo/map], clip.a000→Camtasia split, unknown.qqq→Unknown); static `out/` served, HTTP 200.
